 "notes": "Boxes are the PDF widgets on every page (the signature and its date have no widgets). Page 0: 'First name and middle initial' joins first + middle name; the transform language cannot take the initial of one joined part, so a full middle name is accepted and only join is required (an extra char_at/slice is fine). Filing status checkboxes c1_1[0..2] map to the three-value enum with equals. Step 3 lines 3(a)/3(b) are pathless: payroll keeps only the Step 3 total. Money boxes take the number as-is (no transform required). 'Employer's name and address' is one box (join). Pathless by design: all widgets on page 2 (Multiple Jobs Worksheet) and page 3 (Deductions Worksheet); they are the employee's own worksheets, not payroll data."
